// Deal or Force - the door through which a deterrent is acquired in play (Deterrence.cs).
//
// The holders of 2024 are authored in common/deterrence; this is how everybody else joins
// the club, which is how proliferation arrives as a consequence rather than a script. The
// effect is a tier, not a share: one point of `deterrence` is tier 1, mutual assured
// destruction, and the war judgement prices a direct war between two holders out of the
// arithmetic from the day it is researched.
//
// A mod for an era before the bomb ships no such technology and an empty holders row, and
// the mechanic never speaks. A mod that wants a different rung - chemical, biological, a
// defence that survives a first strike - names its own technology with its own cost and
// the same effect key.
{
  "nuclear_deterrence": {
    "name": "Nuclear deterrence",
    "description": "A deterrent of our own design and our own keeping: nobody attacks us directly again, and we do not attack them.",
    "category": "military", "cost": 400,
    "effects": { "deterrence": 1 }
  }
}
